    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Inversion in a Circle" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="16" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="Reflected across a line, the grid flips over and its lines stay straight. Reflected in a circle (called inversion), it turns inside out and its lines bend into arcs.\n\nEach point P goes to the point P′ on the ray from O through P where\nOP · OP′ = r²\nHere [OP] · [dist(O, P')] = [OP * dist(O, P')] = [r]².\n\nOutside goes inside, inside goes outside, and the circle itself stays put. A line that misses O becomes a circle through O; a line through O stays a line.\n\nA shiny Christmas ornament does something similar: it squeezes the whole room into the ball and curves its straight edges. Its formula is different, but the idea is the same.\n\nDrag P and B to move the grid, O and r to change the circle, M and N to tilt the mirror line. To invert figures of your own, pick Reflect on the Transform tab and click a circle as the mirror." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="64" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true">
      <Dependency Name="O" />
      <Dependency Name="P" />
      <Dependency Name="P'" />
      <Dependency Name="r" />
    </Label>
